	(gr_text_box "PCBWay stackup and adapted trace dimensions defined in /workspaces/STM32WLE5_RF_dongle/hw/PCBWay/W1090617AS5P1-stackup & impedance control file.pdf\n\nWith the selected stackup, 50 ohm differential impedance cannot be achieved using edge-coupled microstrip within PCBWay standard limits. If needed, route both traces as nominal 50 Ohm single-ended microstrips, keep them short and symmetric, and do not apply a controlled differential-pair constraint.\n\nUse B.Cu (bottom) for low-speed, non-impedance-controlled signals only.\n\nGeneral power traces --> 0.5mm width\nDevice specific power traces --> 0.2mm width\n\n0.56mm via diameter and 0.25mm via hole for generic vias\n0.7mm via diameter and 0.3mm via hole for general power vias"
